{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011524-red-light-green-light","id":1011524,"title":"Red Light / Green Light","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-03T09:12:21-08:00","id":1011524,"title":"Red Light / Green Light","content":"This is minor, but it's been annoying me for a while. Does anyone else think that the Time spell &quot;Red Light / Green Light&quot; should be a Fate spell? The description sure looks like a Fate spell to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T09:13:48-08:00","id":1011528,"title":"","content":"It's a Time spell because it affects timing of events. You could also create a Fate spell that does the same thing because it would be affecting probability of all those events aligning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T10:19:13-08:00","id":1011551,"title":"","content":"Remember that the same basic effect can often be accomplished by more than one Arcanum. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T10:45:51-08:00","id":1011569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011524-red-light-green-light?p=1011551#post1011551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that the same basic effect can often be accomplished by more than one Arcanum.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that, but this seems to be effecting change via the same methods of a fate spell. It is causing things around you to play out toward a specific goal, regardless of whether the word 'timing&quot; is used or not. Casting a spell that lets you see or adjust the speed of cars around you so your drive to the grocery store is faster - that nakes sense to me. Casting a spell on someone so every elevator he comes across and every traffic line he deals with, (even though you as the caster didn't know these things would necessarily be in his path) slows or speeds to impede his trip to the grocery store does not seem to be in the purview of Time. Not as a single level 1 spell anyway.<br /> <br /> It's hardly a game breaker or anything, but since I've always felt that Fate and Time step on each other's toes enough as it is, it feels wrong to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T11:00:16-08:00","id":1011580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011524-red-light-green-light?p=1011569#post1011569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's hardly a game breaker or anything, but since I've always felt that Fate and Time step on each other's toes enough as it is, it feels wrong to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that among the Ruling Arcana pairs, there's probably the greatest overlap and gray areas between Time and Fate, and that the Green Light / Red Light spell can easily be conceived as an effect from either Arcanum. <br /> <br /> While I personally am not bothered by the spell as an example of a Time effect, I doubt anyone would question your group making it a &quot;primary&quot; Fate effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T12:09:54-08:00","id":1011608,"title":"","content":"It does seem pretty Fate-like to me. I could see a Time spell speeding up or slowing down time on <i>a particular</i> traffic light or elevator or whatever to help or hinder someone in getting where they need to go. Or a Fate spell that increases or decreases the probability of the subject getting caught in traffic or otherwise delayed. But for a spell to basically follow the subject, recognize when ever their subject is about to encounter machinery that runs on a timer, assess whether the machine's timer needs to be sped up or slowed down to affect the subject's travel in the desired way, and execute that, repeatedly, until the duration expires... That's an incredibly complex, and arguably intelligent spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T13:18:57-08:00","id":1011629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011524-red-light-green-light?p=1011608#post1011608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does seem pretty Fate-like to me. I could see a Time spell speeding up or slowing down time on <i>a particular</i> traffic light or elevator or whatever to help or hinder someone in getting where they need to go. Or a Fate spell that increases or decreases the probability of the subject getting caught in traffic or otherwise delayed. But for a spell to basically follow the subject, recognize when ever their subject is about to encounter machinery that runs on a timer, assess whether the machine's timer needs to be sped up or slowed down to affect the subject's travel in the desired way, and execute that, repeatedly, until the duration expires... That's an incredibly complex, and arguably intelligent spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me it seems Boolean, honestly. Yes, you arrive on time, or No, you don't. How either occurs is based purely on synchronous behavior that you, and everyone around you, experiences daily. But rather than shifting complex systems in real time, it just sets you on a path of rapid or stagnant response to these systems as you happen upon them.<br /> <br /> My explanation makes it sounds much more Fate-y than I thought it would. From a Time perspective, I would call the spell still a Compelling Practice because it Compels Time to do what it already can do by itself: Set a course for future events to happen. You thicken Time for someone, and render it in stone for the subject to then experience it in a simple, yet broad scope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8573,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","user":"Zombiecakes","date":". 12-03-2016, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T13:55:52-08:00","id":1011650,"title":"","content":"Assuming the street lights work at set intervals, Time fits better than Fate. The spell doesn't manipulate causality, it alters a countdown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T14:23:16-08:00","id":1011662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011524-red-light-green-light?p=1011650#post1011650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming the street lights work at set intervals, Time fits better than Fate. The spell doesn't manipulate causality, it alters a countdown.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but how does it know when to do that and whether to speed it up or slow it down? Aren't intelligent spells supposed to be an Archmastery thing?<br /> <br /> Like I said, making a light turn red or green early or late makes perfect sense for Time to me. Assessing whether each light someone comes to needs to be changed and whether it needs to be sped up or slowed down to accomplish that, on the other hand, seems far more complicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-03-2016, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T16:45:03-08:00","id":1011734,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't go so far as to assume that the spell is assessing anything, it's an automatic process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T16:51:16-08:00","id":1011739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011524-red-light-green-light?p=1011734#post1011734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't go so far as to assume that the spell is assessing anything, it's an automatic process.</div> </div> </div> </div>It clearly must have some form of discretion though. if it knows which lights to make change faster and which ones to make change slower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T17:14:27-08:00","id":1011747,"title":"","content":"I don't think it actually changes the lights or the timing on them so much as it influences the target's rate of travel in relation to the timing that the lights have. In that sense it's really not that different from cruise control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T20:04:29-08:00","id":1011800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011524-red-light-green-light?p=1011747#post1011747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it actually changes the lights or the timing on them so much as it influences the target's rate of travel in relation to the timing that the lights have. In that sense it's really not that different from cruise control.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... Not what the spell description suggests, in my opinion. But alright, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T05:57:48-08:00","id":1011966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011524-red-light-green-light?p=1011747#post1011747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it actually changes the lights or the timing on them so much as it influences the target's rate of travel in relation to the timing that the lights have. In that sense it's really not that different from cruise control.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the purposes of this discussion I don't see that it matters whether the spell adjusts the speed of each light/elevator/crowd that the subject encounters or adjusts the subjects speed relative to same. Either way it seems it needs fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T06:13:35-08:00","id":1011978,"title":"","content":"It doesn't seem that way to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T06:33:54-08:00","id":1011991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011524-red-light-green-light?p=1011978#post1011978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't seem that way to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>If someone was to cast &quot;Velocity Control&quot; as a deleterious effect on an enemy, and state that for the duration he wanted the spell to show the subject down when he was being chased by something dangerous, and to speed the subject up when he was running toward something dangerous, I would look at it the same way I look at this spell. Admittedly Red Light / Green Light won't ruin anyone's game, and as Branford suggested I can just toss it into Fate for my games (or disallow its ability to affect another subject as described).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T06:37:04-08:00","id":1011992,"title":"","content":"I'd just do that if I were you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}